script:post-response {
  const data = res.getBody() && res.getBody().data;
  if (data) {
    if (data.id) bru.setEnvVar("tenantId", data.id);
    if (data.slug) bru.setEnvVar("tenantSlug", data.slug);
    // The admin's login phone is returned; the password is the one supplied in
    // the request (no temp password is generated), so capture it from the body.
    const phone = data.adminPhone || (data.admin && data.admin.phone);
    if (phone) bru.setEnvVar("adminPhone", phone);
    const body = req.getBody && req.getBody();
    if (body && body.adminPassword) bru.setEnvVar("adminPassword", body.adminPassword);
  }
}

docs {
  Create a tenant (business) **and** its first business-admin user. Requires
  `business:create` (operations_admin and above).

  The first admin is registered as a full tenant staff member (a
  `TenantStaffMembership` with `userCode` `USR-00001`, flagged `isPrimaryAdmin`),
  so they appear in — and can be managed from — the business **Users** list
  (assign branches/modules/permissions). This primary admin can never be
  deactivated.

  The business-admin's login **password is chosen in the request** (`adminPassword`)
  and stored as a non-temp password, so nothing sensitive is returned. The script
  captures `tenantId`, `tenantSlug`, `adminPhone`, and echoes `adminPassword` from
  the request body — used by **Business Auth → Login**.

  Fields:
  - `name` (required) — business name.
  - `slug` (optional) — lowercase alphanumeric + hyphens, not at start/end
    (subdomain `{slug}.kalnostics.com`). When omitted, a unique slug is
    auto-generated from `name`.
  - `adminFirstName` (required) — first business-admin's first name.
  - `adminMiddleName` (optional) — admin's middle name.
  - `adminLastName` (optional) — admin's last name.
  - `adminPhone` (required) — admin's globally-unique login identifier; a plain
    **10-digit** mobile number (no `+91`/country code).
  - `adminEmail` (optional) — admin's email (globally unique if set).
  - `adminPassword` (**required**) — the admin's login password. Policy: min 8
    chars, ≥1 uppercase, ≥1 digit.
  - `email` (optional) — tenant contact email.
  - `phone` (optional) — tenant contact phone.
  - `shortName` (optional) — business abbreviation.
  - `addressLine` (optional) — street address.
  - `pincode` (optional) — zip / pin code.
  - `countryId` / `stateId` / `cityId` / `areaId` (optional) — location hierarchy
    ids from **Location Data**. Any subset is allowed but must be consistent
    (an area's city/state/country must match the supplied ids) or the request is
    rejected with a hierarchy-mismatch error.
  - `logoUrl` / `photoUrl` (optional) — media URL strings.
  - `address` (optional) — free-form JSON object (legacy; structured fields above
    are preferred).
  - `mrnPrefix` (optional) — patient MRN prefix (e.g. "AC" -> "AC-00001").
  - `settings` (**required**) — locale JSON. `timezone` and `currency` are
    **required** and validated against the supported shortlists (an unsupported
    value is rejected with 400). `date_format` / `language` are optional and
    fall back to platform defaults (`DD/MM/YYYY`, `en`). Supported `timezone`
    values include `UTC`, `Asia/Kolkata`, `Asia/Dubai`, `Europe/London`,
    `America/New_York`, `America/Los_Angeles`, `Australia/Sydney` (see
    `SUPPORTED_TIMEZONES`); supported `currency` values include `INR`, `USD`,
    `GBP`, `EUR`, `AED`, `SGD`, `AUD` (see `SUPPORTED_CURRENCIES`). Keys:
    `timezone` (required), `currency` (required), `date_format`, `language`,
    `logo_url`, `primary_color`, `secondary_color`, `app_name`.
}
